    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1419">

                <pb facs="0936" n="820" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg820"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.52/308.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Special Agent Carothers.</hi><anchor n="123"
                        xml:id="d1419-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-06-08">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 8, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Spanish Ambassador, this city, by direction of his Sovereign, has requested the
                    Department to use its good offices to prevent Constitutionalists from enforcing
                    loan of 500,000 pesos demanded of Spaniards at Tampico.</p>
                <p>Bring to attention of Carranza, stating that this is done at request of
                    Ambassador and urge that no discriminatory or confiscatory action be taken
                    against Spaniards.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. J. Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1419-f1" n="123" type="source" xml:id="d1419-f1-content">
                <p>Similar telegram to the American Consul at Tampico.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
